  "details": "Originally filed this as an SDK bug, but decided it probably belongs under client bugs so I deleted that canny and copied it here.\n\nAs the title implies, if you upload a world with the VRC Scene Descriptor component attached to a disabled object, the result will be a performance degradation.\n\nI'm not talking a small difference either, I'm talking \"I went down to 20fps in desktop mode on my 1080p monitor that's being fed by a 3090 and everyone that joined my instance could also immediately feel the change\" kinda difference.\n\nI'm not sure if uploading in this state causes an object to be toggling on/off every frame or what, but it the stutter it causes *feels* like that kind of thing.\n\nYou may think it strange that anyone would upload their project with the VRCWorld object disabled, and it is, I happened upon this by accident. But still, I think this should either be fixed so that you can safely upload it in such a way, or it simply shouldn't allow people to upload their world in such a state to begin with.\n\nThanks.",
